direction: down
"derived-credit": "derived-credit\nHandler publishes native reason or transfers failure\ncustody before last old-route access; count zero is\nnot work closure"
"entry": "entry\nPermanent trampoline uses one tagged lock-free\nadmission/refcount CAS before dereferencing route or\nendpoint; paused pre-CAS handler is uncounted but\nharmless"
"revoke": "revoke\nClose same atomic admission gate first; late\nhandlers cannot acquire old generation; do not\nconfuse disposition update with grace completion"
"storage-commit": "storage-commit\nRetire old route/native endpoint only after\nadmission closed, active pins zero, work/fault debt\nzero and old-roster receipt; stable shell outlives\nVM"
"masks": "masks\nTrack actual calling-thread mask and normalized\nresults; thread roster/birth fence needed for any\nall-thread claim; masking is not route reclamation\nauthority"
"failure": "failure\nUnknown mask/disposition/wake result retains\ncoordinator and delivery custody; no false drain\nacknowledgement or blocking of GC roles"
"participant": "participant\nDrain while old roster/root/finite-wait services\nremain alive; caller POSIX mask is distinct from\nScheme sync-op service mask"
"mailbox": "mailbox\nDenied or ambiguous late signal goes to process-\nlifetime native mailbox, not stale VM pointer or\nautomatic next-generation replay; preserve reason\npolicy"
"entry" -> "revoke"
"revoke" -> "storage-commit"
"derived-credit" -> "storage-commit"
"failure" -> "storage-commit"
"participant" -> "storage-commit"
"mailbox" -> "entry"
"masks" -> "failure"
"derived-credit" -> "participant"
"derived-credit" -> "mailbox"
"mailbox" -> "storage-commit"
proof: "SysML -> ASCENT -> QNT / Lean; source + platform OPEN"
"storage-commit" -> proof
gain0: "retirement\nA selected pre-CAS handler may be denied after route\nretirement; every legacy bypass must first migrate"
proof -> gain0
gain1: "latency\nProgress requires handler termination, scheduler/OS\nfairness and prior wake protocol; no measured speedup"
proof -> gain1
gain2: "ownership\nO(R+H+T) route/active-handler/thread-policy metadata;\nprocess shell cannot be reclaimed by individual VM"
proof -> gain2
gain3: "language\nZig cannot remove signal ABI, root lifetime, grace or\nsemantic ownership proofs; no mandatory incremental\nbenefit established"
proof -> gain3
